    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 195,
        "text": "Okay, everyone, thanks for coming back after lunch. We have forty minutes to decide whether we keep our original hypothesis or revise it. Let's start with the numbers from the second trial.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "3a58dbda8c819dcc60cdb0b926ca399370b7001c00e4aaf54d66e886aff20f14",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 205,
        "sourceEnd": 401,
        "text": "Right. The first trial showed a clear increase in recall when students studied in short blocks. But the second trial, with the larger group, showed almost no difference. Honestly, I was surprised.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "ea910e892e46b5a18fd0e5bbd1a235313242eddb19fa2cba0b67cc8f1ea2e046",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 409,
        "sourceEnd": 562,
        "text": "So the two trials disagree. Before we panic, let's check the conditions. Daniel, were the participants in the second trial given the same amount of time?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "f42d67bb972624a258205b5994feaccf2d785191bd20605758073b6903e22abd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 572,
        "sourceEnd": 712,
        "text": "Not exactly. The second group had ten extra minutes, but they also had more distractions in the room. Two people were talking near the door.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "dc49c9b783b49ad17c974c772847cced9721e56f90a71fe18499125a2187cb13",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 721,
        "sourceEnd": 877,
        "text": "Sorry to interrupt — I think that matters. If the room was noisier, then the second trial didn't really test the same thing. We can't compare them directly.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "265bf9c2de8f2b454bc4334e85092da78b6c49ba2df3bd7432c7e2cc56272ede",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 885,
        "sourceEnd": 955,
        "text": "Good point. So what do we do with the hypothesis? Do we throw it away?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "e0343c42efd5e11b95904773473baa9cd93692e60994f3d461ebbbeb668f8330",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 964,
        "sourceEnd": 1110,
        "text": "No, I wouldn't throw it away. I'd narrow it. Maybe short blocks help only when the room is quiet. That's a smaller claim, but it fits both trials.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "7db883c507e964727a421af1aa1f00a57f277592b52418da2d5e6303259289bd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1120,
        "sourceEnd": 1244,
        "text": "Hmm. I see what you mean, but I'm not fully convinced. The first trial was small — only twelve students. Twelve is not many.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "f36e46a410a6125039d4cc70f14896a4524332f736c6a4d60283449ab816e609",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1252,
        "sourceEnd": 1361,
        "text": "That's fair. So we have two problems: a small first sample and a noisy second room. Neither trial is perfect.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "3ef0530a335c5f413bba7836a759bb290967f5e01fd14ca9e7b0d7c33911c2a2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1370,
        "sourceEnd": 1600,
        "text": "Can I suggest something? Let's revise the hypothesis to include the noise condition, and then run a third trial with thirty students in a quiet room. If the effect appears again, we keep the revised hypothesis. If not, we drop it.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "da05993cd6ac2ad207de5810fb4e63f6320453665a476152e34c61bc3138b0f6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1610,
        "sourceEnd": 1660,
        "text": "Wait — thirty? I thought we agreed on twenty-five.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "988ecf94ece1da207612cfe4f0bb3b7f18eaae3d63e68c2885bd6f8227bafec3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1668,
        "sourceEnd": 1786,
        "text": "We did say twenty-five earlier, but Priya's thirty gives us a safer margin. I'm happy with thirty if everyone else is.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "60ec77c4496b7aa046e6c6d3f04cc1f5fff076bc9054e47b7c7c77f505a64ee3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1796,
        "sourceEnd": 1863,
        "text": "Okay, thirty works for me. But who is going to book the quiet room?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "9e3a8121101c7e67a58d4efd13be28dfc8633d315401f9a4c4e5c730d7239df4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1872,
        "sourceEnd": 1981,
        "text": "I can ask the library. They have a small seminar room on the second floor. It's usually free in the mornings.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "7734c240f53d80a16893122556b4510d6f212ab73ad4eb84f64695afcb8c39b1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1989,
        "sourceEnd": 2175,
        "text": "Perfect. So, to confirm: we revise the hypothesis, we add the noise condition, and we run a third trial with thirty students in a quiet room. Daniel, can you write that up before Friday?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "d7f7274e659413dd8b09d08edcad7f6e60ac838bcb955e78d8903e1194502ac4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2185,
        "sourceEnd": 2249,
        "text": "Yes, I'll send a short summary to the group by Thursday evening.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "941d14e8431ea248ca7265f79cf8efc7a0a743e78ec84157404fc2adf01a0b71",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 2258,
        "sourceEnd": 2335,
        "text": "One more thing — should we tell the first twelve students about the revision?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "ab04403cd67161a41cb8d64f45f99dc0436b326172eab793759c5c5d90bd19f6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2343,
        "sourceEnd": 2487,
        "text": "Good question. I think we should, briefly. They took part, so they deserve to know what we concluded. But we won't ask them to do anything more.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "285de602ad19673151cb63d1348d83c039f04f26b82a9747682b2c28cda087ab",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2497,
        "sourceEnd": 2590,
        "text": "Agreed. And I'll note in the summary that the first trial was small, so nobody over-reads it.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "a7b5c8361cb1cd5d2a293edf238b2cf0b74cca7c4907314dbbe23949585aca6a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2598,
        "sourceEnd": 2639,
        "text": "Great. Then we're done. Thanks, everyone.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "51278eacaf662735c444c1ab04b89321908c4178cc5de6fb4b36ea19af74eb87",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
